{sov: Notes}
Pocket over Chords: The track is built on a tight, deep-pocket 16th-note funk
groove in D Dorian. Keep chord embellishments light and percussive—staccato
stabs work far better than sustained strumming.

Main Vamp: The rhythm section rides the Dm7 statically, using a subtle slide
or passing step down to C/D (or C7/D) on beat 4 to create the classic '70s-
style raw funk tension.

Horn Break: When the horns hit the turnaround, switch to punchy 9th chord
voicings (F9 to G9) on the upbeats before resolving directly back to the root
Dm7 groove.

Guitar Voicings: Favor top-4-string triad and 7th shell voicings to stay out
of the bass and organ register.
{eov}